WEBVTT

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.490
The National Vanguard Championship.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.300
We're seeing passionate fights breaking out,

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.780
and winning teams breaking 
through the preliminary blocks!

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.950
The first qualifying fight...

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.080
was lost...

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.270
And without even one match won...

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:29.030
Brother...

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:42.150
Maybe if I had stayed with the team, 
the result would've been different...

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:48.360
But I just can't fight 
on the same team as Kai!

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.570
I can't go back...

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:58.070
When the Moon is Full

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.530
Team Q4       Team Jurassic Army
Team Muscle Brain       Team FFAL4

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.300
There are three fights in 
the elimination round...

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.080
The top two highest-ranking 
teams in each block

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.950
can go on to the next 
round of the tournament.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.370
We can't afford to lose any more.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.850
So he'll be in the finals.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:24.660
You'll probably be able to meet 
him if you make it to the finals.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:27.640
Ren...

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.350
Kai!

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:34.070
Um... I thought maybe we could talk 
over the order for the next fight...

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.990
Do as you please. I don't 
care which match I'm in.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:40.340
Okay. Got it...

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:47.680
That was my first fight since deciding

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.660
to seriously focus on Vanguard.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.420
I want to win...

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.340
Win... and then...

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:11.470
There are some things they have 
to learn by themselves...

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.930
Manager...

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.540
Um... About the order for the next fight...

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.900
That should be okay.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.820
But I haven't said anything yet...

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.500
Kai goes first...

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:24.760
Right?

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:27.100
Y-Yes...

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.780
The idea is,

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:33.260
he'll win the first match, and then 
either Misaki or I will win ours.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.620
Is that being too timid?

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.660
Yeah, incredibly...

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:41.520
But I think that's fine.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:47.500
After recognizing your own weakness, 
you pondered the best strategy.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:51.000
That's one way to fight as a team.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.250
I see...

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:59.110
Okay, then Kai will go first, Misaki 
second, and Aichi will be third.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:00.540
We're all agreed?

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:10.180
The Vanguard National Championship...

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:14.600
Even in the qualifying round, all of the 
blocks are engaged in fierce fights!

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:15.790
I'm so excited!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.890
And now, continuing with 
Elimination Round Block A,

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.970
we have Team Q4 versus Team Muscle Brain!

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:23.780
Indeed!

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.280
This is a showdown between 
both teams that have one loss!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.590
Which one will win and open 
the way to the finals?!

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:37.340
According to the member roster, Q4 is...

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:42.460
Kai Toshiki, Tokura Misaki, and Sendou Aichi.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.200
Team Muscle Brain is...

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.950
Are these their real names?

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.680
Well, whatever...

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.400
Kick Shuu...

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.940
Punch Ken...

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:54.170
Groundwork... Snake...

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:58.870
This makes sense. Their motto is...

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:02.200
The strongest brains residing 
in the strongest bodies!

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.120
I suppose...

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.850
Under that principle, to become the number 
one Vanguard Fighters in the nation,

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:11.620
they train their bodies 
as well as their brains.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.190
Let's count on a heated battle!

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.260
In this first match,

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.740
Kai Toshiki versus Kick Shuu!

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.760
Do you wanna know my hobby?

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:22.580
Not particularly.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.970
Well, I'll tell you.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:26.170
It's breaking bats with my kicks!

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.880
Three bats a day, a thousand bats a year!

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.000
And I'm gonna break you, too!

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.400
That would cost you a great deal.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:33.120
Wha...?!

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.070
Kai, please!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.220
So Kai is going first...

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.550
At least get one win.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.950
At this rate, I'll be embarrassed 
to hang out at the same shop.

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:49.320
Can't you just cheer them on?!

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.330
Although Kai hardly ever loses...

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:56.400
Begin the match!

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.280
Stand up the Vanguard!

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.280
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.210
Nova Grappler...

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:23.420
Since I know the characteristics of that deck 
inside and out, I would've won this hands down!

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.890
I ride Blazing Core Dragon!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.420
I call Gattling Claw Dragon!

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.860
Blazing Core's Counterblast!

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.940
Iron Tail and Gattling Claw move 
from the rear-guard circle to the Soul.

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.350
Then...

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.400
Three sealed gods of destruction...

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.320
gain the power of explosive flames and rise!

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:58.660
I superior ride Blazing Flare Dragon!

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:03.430
What?! Even though you went second, 
you're bringing out a grade 3 first?!

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.710
On top of that, I call Nehalem!

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:17.010
I attack King of Sword with Blazing Flare!

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:18.930
Twin drive check!

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:19.920
As always, total lack of charm!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.990
Got it! Critical trigger!

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:23.990
All you can do is feel 
sympathy for the other guy...

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:30.450
I attack with Overlord 
and a powered-up Nehalem!

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:34.420
Overlord!

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.230
Nehalem!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.170
I guard with this!

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:45.410
5 damage already...?

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.300
Dang! I hate to admit it, but he's strong...

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.270
Final Turn!

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.000
I call Demonic Dragon Mage, Kimnara!

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:58.130
Counterblast.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.620
Kimnara moves to the Soul.

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:04.590
Now I can retire one of your grade 
1 units from the rear-guard!

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:05.870
Tough Boy!

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:11.820
And whenever I retire one 
of my opponent's units,

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.860
Blazing Flare's power increases by +3000!

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:19.290
And then, Soulblast!

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:27.160
I retire one of your units 
from the rear-guard...

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.440
Hungry Dumpty!

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:36.050
With that, Blazing Flare's 
power again increases by +3000!

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.500
With a boost from Conroe...

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.770
Blazing Flare attacks!

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:59.100
The winner, from Team Q4...

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:00.500
Kai Toshiki!

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:04.140
Wonderful!

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.710
Kai, the out-and-out victor!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.810
So far, this is Q4's first win!

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:11.770
That certainly was exciting, wasn't it?

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:14.060
Great job, Kai.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.760
You're so strong, Kai! That was amazing!

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.550
A win is a win.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:20.300
No matter what form it takes...

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:27.400
Kai isn't touched at all 
by anxiety or pressure...

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:30.810
All right, let's move on to the second match!

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.650
Please do your best, Misaki!

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:36.290
Hey, you okay?

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:40.370
No good... Instead of a bat, it 
looks like his heart is broken.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.850
Suck it up.

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:43.920
I'll win with my punch!

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.320
Poor guy...

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:47.310
Yep...

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:49.610
The next match is starting!

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.940
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:58.370
Prepare yourself!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:03.360
This fist that's been built up by pounding 
sand every day... will crush you to pieces!

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:04.910
I ride Tough Boy!

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.630
Battleraizer moves!

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:11.600
He's got a Nova Grappler deck, too...

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.960
Don't let your guard down!

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.040
I'm not drawing any grade 3s...

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:20.380
I activate Godhawk, 
Ichibyoshi's skill!

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.490
I look at the top five cards of my deck,

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:25.790
and if Goddess of the Crescent Moon, 
Tsukuyomi, is among them,

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.950
I can do a superior ride!

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.500
So that's how you're comin' at me!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.980
The other four cards go 
to the bottom of the deck.

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:35.710
I call Oracle Guardian, Gemini...

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.730
and Psychic Bird!

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:42.000
With a boost from Psychic Bird...

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.420
Tsukuyomi attacks!

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.950
Drive trigger check.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.770
Damage trigger check!

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:54.990
I attack with Gemini!

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.240
Damage trigger check!

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:02.200
2 damage. That's a good start!

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:05.160
That was a nice punch.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.970
Thanks for the damage.

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:09.510
This puts me right on the 
path to certain victory.

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.850
I ride King of Sword!

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:14.960
And call Karma Queen!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.400
Megacolony?!

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:17.860
He's got a mixed deck!

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:19.200
MD, yo!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.430
Then it's not a pure Nova Grappler deck!

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.960
Karma's Counterblast!

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:28.700
One of your rear-guard units won't 
be able to stand next turn...

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.690
Gemini! You!

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:33.950
I call Clay-doll Mechanic!

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:41.930
With Clay-doll's skill, I can flip 
over one card in the Damage Zone!

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:44.800
And then I call one more Clay-doll Mechanic!

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.300
I activate its skill!

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:50.100
Now I can do a Counterblast one more time!

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:53.090
He's got a good grasp 
of Nova Grappler traits!

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:54.920
Not as good as mine, but...

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:57.800
Feel my powerful punch!

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.550
A left hook from Karma!

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:01.870
Damage check...

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.670
A straight punch from King!

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:07.530
Drive trigger check!

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.520
Damage check...

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:14.810
Clay-doll Mechanic gets a boost from the other 
Clay-doll Mechanic, and gives you a right uppercut!

00:13:15.650 --> 00:13:17.480
Damage trigger check...

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:19.780
Draw trigger!

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:21.810
I draw...

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:26.200
You powered up for nothing, huh?

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.350
This time for sure...

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:52.110
Not the one...

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.800
I activate the skill of Goddess 
of the Crescent Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.680
I look at the top five cards of my deck...

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:02.040
and if one of them is Goddess of the Half 
Moon, Tsukuyomi, I can do a superior ride.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:03.680
It's not here.

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:08.570
Ain't nothin' better than hitting 
you with a barrage of lucky punches!

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:12.200
Well, sure... But you can't 
stop the flow of time.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.540
The moon always waxes...

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.830
I ride Goddess of the Half Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.860
You had that?!

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:29.310
In this instance, if Crescent Moon and Godhawk are 
in the Soul, I can Soulcharge two cards!

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:32.100
Psychic Bird's skill!

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.480
I put it in the Soul and draw one card!

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:36.640
Still hasn't come up...

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.820
Looks like things aren't going 
the way you want them to.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:40.250
I move Gemini.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.280
Wha...?! Don't ignore me!

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:46.240
I call two Silent Toms 
and Weather Girl, Milk!

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.800
With a boost from Milk...

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.410
Tsukuyomi attacks!

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:52.340
Milk's skill adds another +4000 to her power!

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:58.460
Drive trigger check!

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.240
Damage trigger check!

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:09.320
As long as Gemini can't stand, all 
I can do is target his rear-guard...

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.400
I attack Karma with Silent Tom!

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:17.930
Silent Tom! Attack Clay-doll Mechanic!

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:23.280
Next... What comes next will decide it!

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:25.150
I ride Gold Rutile!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:29.600
I ride Death Metal Droid and Karma Queen!

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:33.610
If you're gonna come at me with Tsukuyomi, 
I'm going after you with Karma Queen!

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.180
Counterblast!

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:38.590
I'm gonna put that pesky Silent Tom to sleep!

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:42.090
She can't stand again...

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:44.440
Death Metal delivers a high-speed jab!

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:52.470
With Gold Rutile's skill, when your 
Vanguard is hit by a rear-guard attack...

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:54.650
I can turn over one card in the Damage Zone!

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:57.110
Why doesn't she guard?

00:15:57.110 --> 00:16:00.180
Maybe she's only got grade 
3 cards in her hand...

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:02.570
Battleraizer boosts!

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:04.460
Here it comes!

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:07.580
A corkscrew punch from Gold Rutile!

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:10.630
Battleraizer's skill adds 
another +3000 to his power!

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.540
I guard with Battle Sister Chocolat!

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.760
<i>This time</i> she's guarding?!

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:19.600
Your attack with Rutile is futile!

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:23.050
Shoot!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:26.770
If Gold Rutile is the Vanguard 
and its attack hits...

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:30.260
the rear-guard can stand with a Counterblast.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.890
The rear-guard can stand?!

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:32.850
Then...

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:38.800
Tokura weighed the risk of it powering up 
with a trigger and nullified the attack...

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:41.180
Twin drive...

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.490
1st check!

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:43.940
2nd check!

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.220
Critical trigger!

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:48.910
I give the power and the 
+1 critical to Karma!

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.930
I'm still on a roll!

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:56.660
Karma, boosted by Clay-doll 
Mechanic, gives a body blow!

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:59.300
I guard with Oracle Guardian, Nike.

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:01.370
Silent Tom intercepts!

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:08.010
Battleraizer returns to the deck...

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:08.750
Yes!

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.160
She held out!

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:12.540
Now it's her turn!

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:13.790
<i>This time</i>...

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:15.690
Still hasn't shown up...

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:17.870
But there's still...

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:19.910
With Tsukuyomi's skill...

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:22.100
I look at the top five cards of my deck.

00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:26.140
One...

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.050
Two...

00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:29.910
You've run out of luck!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.920
The Moon Goddess...

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.290
Wow!

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:39.670
Three...

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:41.420
Four...

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:45.610
I'll take good care of it...

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:47.670
Dad and Mom!

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:49.740
Five...

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:05.130
N-No way...

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:08.850
Gentle light that illuminates the darkness...

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:11.540
Your smile will envelop the world...

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:14.950
I superior ride Goddess of 
the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.500
Goddess of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi...

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:26.510
Misaki's managed two superior 
rides in one fight?!

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:40.340
Goddess of the Full Moon, 
Tsukuyomi's Counterblast!

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:44.620
I draw two cards from my deck and put 
one card from my hand into the Soul.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.400
And then, one more Counterblast!

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.150
Increasing the number of cards in your hand

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:57.310
doesn't have any effect on the 
number of times you can attack!

00:18:57.310 --> 00:18:59.230
My damage is 3.

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:02.580
I'll protect myself, then give you 
a KO punch as the coup de grace!

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.660
I call CEO Amaterasu and Gemini!

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:08.500
Tsukuyomi attacks with a boost from Milk!

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:15.050
Twin drive...

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:19.440
Draw trigger!

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.780
Amaterasu's power increases by +5000!

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.160
And then I draw!

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:33.970
Damage trigger check!

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:37.290
Amaterasu attacks with a boost from Gemini!

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:40.040
I guard with two Red Lightnings!

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:43.620
Silent Tom attacks with a boost from Gemini!

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:49.740
5 damage...

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.670
But I'm still here!

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:54.570
I'm rushing into the last round!

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:57.200
I'm gonna knock you out with my punch!

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.130
Knock out?

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:03.310
Six cards in my hand and 
one interceptor unit...

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.450
So if you can break through these cards...

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:13.650
Ken! You can still come 
from behind with a KO!

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:14.950
Forget about it!

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:16.120
This is a done deal!

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.590
Oh, yeah!

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:20.180
Karma exits the field and I call Death Metal!

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.870
With a boost from Clay-doll 
Mechanic, Death Metal attacks!

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:25.630
And an activated skill on top 
of that adds +3000 to his power!

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:27.490
I guard with Lozenge Magus!

00:20:27.860 --> 00:20:30.160
I attack with Gold Rutile!

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.610
I guard with Lozenge!

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:33.160
Twin drive...

00:20:34.220 --> 00:20:35.770
Critical trigger!

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:39.070
I give everything to my other Death Metal!

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:41.280
If I hit her with this attack...

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:45.100
Boosted by Clay-doll Mechanic, 
Death Metal attacks!!

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.440
I guard with Chocolat.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.170
I dropped one card and 
got the perfect defense.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.740
Misaki is incredible...

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:58.480
Final Turn!

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:01.700
I attack with Amaterasu, boosted by Gemini!

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:05.140
Everything rides on a heal trigger...

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:06.360
Check!

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:11.360
She did it! Tokura Misaki of Team Q4!

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:12.880
She did a great job!

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:18.370
With a score of 2-0, Team Q4 is the winner!

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:24.250
She held on by increasing 
the cards in her hand...

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:27.440
That Goddess of the Full Moon, Tsukuyomi,

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:28.680
became the trump card.

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:34.590
Dad, Mom...

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:37.110
I'm doing okay.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:41.880
Even now, Vanguard is a family tie.

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:52.100
With one win and one loss, it's now possible 
for Team Q4 to get through the elimination round!

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:53.690
All that's left is one more fight.

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:56.760
That result will determine which 
teams break out of the block!

00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:01.600
However, waiting for Q4...

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:05.960
is the team that's undefeated with two 
wins today, last year's national champion team...

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:09.330
Foo Fighter AL4!

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:53.100
Misaki, you were fantastic!

00:23:53.100 --> 00:23:54.480
Well, thank you.

00:23:54.480 --> 00:23:55.840
I've gotta do my best, too!

00:23:55.840 --> 00:23:58.820
Um, our next opponents are AL4...

00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:01.580
The strongest team, led by Suzugamori Ren!

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:02.910
I'll do my best, too.

00:24:02.910 --> 00:24:05.200
I hope Kamui comes back, don't you?

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:05.880
Uh-huh!

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:10.560
Next time, I wanna have Kai go first again, and 
then you or I can somehow win our match, Misaki.

00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:13.230
Next time: The Strongest Team, AL4!

00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:16.950
Yes, and to start, try 
to visualize victory...

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:18.740
I think that's a good way to think!
